  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Consider the quadratic equation \(y=x^2-4x\). Consider the graph of the equation when answering questions a and b.</item>
</list>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Where are the \(x\)-intercepts located? </para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>The \(x\)-intercepts are at \(x=0\) and \(x=4\).</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="e6a309ae-6a3f-4fe0-9e91-72ed111a9b04" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="167a80b4-40da-4f97-8af6-067a60705252" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="2">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
        <para>Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The vertex is halfway between the intercepts at \(x=2\).</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
